; Numbers around the 64-bit limit: the largest 64-bit number is 9223372036854775807 and the smallest is
; -9223372036854775808. Sums, products through @ and @@, inferred prices and an elided amount cross it and come back.
2026-01-01 the largest 64-bit number and one more, the elided amount is the smallest
    a  9223372036854775807 X
    b  1 X
    c

2026-01-02 the smallest 64-bit number written, and its negation elided
    a  -9223372036854775808 X
    b

2026-01-03 a sum past the limit, a small result
    a  9223372036854775807 X
    b  9223372036854775807 X
    c  -18446744073709551614 X
    d  3 X
    e

2026-01-04 a product past the limit through @
    a  4294967296 X @ 4294967296 Y
    b  -18446744073709551616 Y

2026-01-05 a total price whose product stays under the limit
    a  3037000499 X @@ 9223372030926249001 Y
    b  -9223372030926249001 Y

2026-01-06 an inferred price that divides a number past the limit by one under it
    a  4611686018427387904 Z
    b  -9223372036854775808 X

2026-01-07 many places on a number near the limit
    a  92233720368547758.07 X
    b  -92233720368547758.07 X
    c  0.0000000000000000001 X
    d  -0.0000000000000000001 X
